<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> Historically our best matchup. We
    assemble the <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opalescence</a
    > plus <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
    > lock faster, and with more backup copies, than a normal Enchantress
    deck can keep up with.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Navigating the Lock:</strong> After sideboard, the main thing
    you have to get through is their protection—usually a couple of <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Sterling Grove">Sterling Grove</a
    >—plus the tax from <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Aura of Silence">Aura of Silence</a
    >. Be patient: hold at least one <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    > or <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Disenchant">Disenchant</a
    > to deal with an incoming <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Decree of Silence">Decree of Silence</a
    > before you go for a game-ending Replenish.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Cut the creature removal you don't
    need (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >) and your anti-land cards (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    >). Bring in extra <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Abeyance"
        >Abeyance</a
    >, and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    >. Since Enchantress tends to load up on graveyard and enchantment hate
    after Game 1, an <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > gives you a great second angle—it just swings through all their hate
    while their hand fills up with dead reactive cards.
</p>
